cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "Muse–Polar: live recording and analysis of Muse 2 EEG and Polar H10 heart data"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Griadhi
    given-names: I Putu Adiartha
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-9895-9353"
    affiliation: "Department of Physiology, Faculty of Medicine, Universitas Udayana, Bali, Indonesia"
repository-code: "https://github.com/adiarthagriadhi/Muse-and-Polar"
abstract: >-
  Open research software that records a Muse 2 EEG headband and a Polar H10 chest strap over
  Bluetooth Low Energy on one host clock (raw CSV, markers, movement-based clock synchronisation,
  simulator) and analyses the recordings (EEG band power per segment, head maps, between-segment
  statistics, PPG pulse-rate variability with the B1 reference pipeline, Polar HRV; EDF/BDF input).
keywords:
  - EEG
  - Muse 2
  - Polar H10
  - photoplethysmography
  - pulse rate variability
  - heart rate variability
  - Bluetooth Low Energy
  - psychophysiology
